{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2599 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3d6fad470fe39b52fda3c41ca18981f42af406e038435af8649aa5348782aba7" :edb/db-before-t 2598 :edb/db-after-t 2599 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535911 50 #inst "2026-10-15T06:45:58.433Z" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540391 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540397 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540415 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540424 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540428 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540431 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1038 #edb/ref 17592186540435 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186229182 1040 #edb/ref 17592186540440 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540391 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540416 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540391 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540391 1071 "A juice-processing tank initially holds $1200\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $22\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved sugar.\nA solution containing $0.04\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of dissolved sugar is pumped into the tank at a rate of $24\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $36\\,\\text{L/min}.$ If the amount of sugar $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins is given by\n\n$$\nQ(t)=\\alpha \\,(1-\\frac{t}{100})+\\beta {(1-\\frac{t}{100})}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants, what is the value of $\\alpha -\\beta ?$" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540391 1072 #uuid "020bf2b5-6b7c-5949-b44d-18f12c8b1668" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540391 1074 "Let $Q$ be the amount of dissolved substance in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. The amount entering minus the amount leaving gives\n$$\\frac{dQ}{dt}=Q'_{\\text{in}}-Q'_{\\text{out}}.$$\nThe units of these rates are $\\text{kg/min}.$\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which substance enters the tank.\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q'_{\\text{in}}&=(0.04\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot(24\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\\\\n&=(0.04\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot(24\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\\\&=0.96\\,\\text{kg/min}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which substance exits the tank.\nThe volume is\n$$V(t)=1200+24t-36t=(1200-12t)\\,\\text{L}.$$\nThe concentration is $\\frac{Q}{1200-12t}\\,\\text{kg/L}.$ Hence,\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q'_{\\text{out}}&=(36\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot(\\frac{Q}{1200-12t}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\\\\n&=(36\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot(\\frac{Q}{1200-12t}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\\\\n&=\\frac{36Q}{1200-12t}\\,\\text{kg/min}=\\frac{3Q}{100-t}\\,\\text{kg/min}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt}&=Q'_{\\text{in}}-Q'_{\\text{out}}\\\\&=0.96-\\frac{3Q}{100-t}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus,\n$$\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{3}{100-t}Q=0.96.$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\nThis is a first-order linear equation with variable coefficients. So we find the general solution using an integrating factor:\n$$\\begin{aligned}I(t)&=e^{\\int 3/(100-t)\\,dt}\\\\&=e^{-3\\ln|100-t|}\\\\&=e^{\\ln (100-t)^{-3}}\\\\&=(100-t)^{-3}.\\end{aligned}$$\nMultiplying both sides by $I(t)=(100-t)^{-3}$ yields\n$$\\begin{aligned}(100-t)^{-3}\\cdot(\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{3}{100-t}Q)&=(100-t)^{-3}\\cdot 0.96\\\\\n(100-t)^{-3}\\frac{dQ}{dt}+3(100-t)^{-4}Q&=0.96(100-t)^{-3}\\\\\\frac{d}{dt}(Q(100-t)^{-3})&=0.96(100-t)^{-3}.\\end{aligned}$$\nNow, we integrate with respect to $t:$\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{d}{dt}(Q(100-t)^{-3})\\,dt&=\\int 0.96(100-t)^{-3}\\,dt\\\\Q(100-t)^{-3}&=0.96\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}(100-t)^{-2}+C\\\\Q(t)&=0.48(100-t)+C(100-t)^{3}.\\end{aligned}$$\nNote that $C$ is a constant of integration.\nThe initial condition is $Q(0)=22.$ Thus,\n$$\\begin{aligned}0.48(100-0)+C(100-0)^{3}&=22\\\\\n48+C(100)^{3}&=22\\\\C(100)^{3}&=-26\\\\C&=- \\frac{13}{500000}.\\end{aligned}$$\nFinally, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n$$Q(t)=- \\frac{12 t}{25} - \\frac{13 \\left(100 - t\\right)^{3}}{500000} + 48.$$\nWriting this in the supplied normalized form gives\n$$Q(t)=48(1-\\frac{t}{100})-26(1-\\frac{t}{100})^{3}.$$\nFinally, we have $\\alpha=48,\\beta=-26,$ and\n$$\\alpha-\\beta=48-(-26)=74.$$" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540392 1080 "13" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540392 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540392 1083 #uuid "02508b23-4879-5a06-8cd4-c201a60347be" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540393 1080 "55" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540393 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540393 1083 #uuid "04ee8d36-4c42-55e1-b036-f809d38523a6" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540401 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540403 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540404 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540406 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1075 #edb/ref 17592186540425 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1077 "selection" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1078 #edb/ref 17592186540403 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540394 1079 #uuid "070c0a32-8846-58e8-a8be-af7c6fd901b8" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540395 1080 "22" 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] [17592186540395 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535911 17592186045443 true] 